# Docker build-context excludes (build context = repo root, see
# infrastructure/docker-compose.yml and packages/data-proxy/Dockerfile).
#
# Two exclusions are load-bearing:
#   - **/node_modules: never copy host node_modules into the image. pnpm's store
#     is symlinked, so a host copy breaks resolution; the image installs fresh via
#     `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
#   - .env.local / .env: never bake secrets (the HMAC token secret, relayer keys)
#     into an image layer.

# Host dependency trees (rebuilt inside the image).
**/node_modules

# Secrets - NEVER baked into an image.
.env
.env.local
**/.env.local
.env.*.local

# Git + local-only planning docs.
.git
.planning

# Build output / generated dirs.
**/dist
# Build OUTPUT only. A bare `**/build` also matches the studio SOURCE directory
# apps/studio/app/components/build (Composer, BuildStream, BuildStepBlock), which strips
# it from the Docker build context and breaks the in-image `pnpm -C apps/studio build`
# (Rollup: could not resolve ../components/build/Composer.js). The only generated build
# dir in this monorepo is apps/studio/build (react-router build); other packages run TS
# directly or emit dist (already excluded). Anchor to a single package segment so nested
# source dirs named build survive the context copy. Do not revert this to `**/build`.
apps/*/build
services/*/build
packages/*/build
**/out
**/.cache
**/.react-router

# Logs and OS cruft.
**/*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Design assets (not needed at runtime).
Design
